id: ops-release-npm-runtime
title: Release and CI install Dependabot locks with the same pinned npm
description: Daily Release run 42412827958 failed before publishing because trusted tool and audit installs used npm 10.9.3 from Node 22.18.0 against the 091124b lock. Standardize release and CI on exact npm 11.21.0 before any locked install.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "gh:unbraind/pm-ops#260"
created_at: "2026-11-07T23:40:56.448Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T09:47:04.110Z"
author: pi-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Inventory every workflow and script npm install with before and after runtimes; Pin and verify npm before trusted tool, provenance and caller installs while retaining node-version and ignore-scripts; PR CI executes the exact release production install against both committed locks; Document passing fixed and failing npm 10.9.3 runs against the unchanged 091124b fixture; Focused tests and typecheck pass; CI is the full gate; docs explain the caller runtime"
comments[50]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-07T23:40:58.995Z",pi-agent,"Repro: on main 091124b (Dependabot #254), npm 10.9.3 ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund reports EUSAGE: glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7. Reported npm 11.17.0 succeeds. CI already selects 11.21.0; release selects 11.19.0 only after tool bootstrap, while audit/alert/recover/Bun hooks inherit bundled npm. Plan: pin packageManager to 11.21.0, install and verify it immediately after setup-node in all reusable jobs, add isolated exact-command root/private PR CI smoke checks, retain lock bytes and lifecycle suppression."
  "2026-11-07T23:44:59.543Z",pi-agent,"Revert proof: immutable 091124b package.json/package-lock.json fixtures on real Node 22.18.0: exact npm ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund exits 1 with npm 10.9.3 (EUSAGE; glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7), exits 0 with npm 11.21.0 (5 production packages). Private provenance fixture passes with both npm versions (52 packages). All four runs preserve the lock SHA-256. In a disposable source copy, retaining new tests/manifests but restoring only both workflows to 091124b gives 0/3 pass and 3 failures; restoring fixed workflows gives 3/3 pass, no skips. Original worktree is never reverted. npm 11.21.0 engine range ^20.17.0 || >=22.9.0 admits the Node 22.18.0 default."
  "2026-11-07T23:45:00.919Z",pi-agent,"Local gates: focused workflow/runtime tests 43/43 pass, zero failures/skips; npm run typecheck and npm run build:test pass; lint passes; duplication 0% (0/37768 lines, 141 sources, zero clones); docstring 48 files/370 declarations pass. Full npm/Bun release gates and Windows consumers are delegated to PR CI per task scope. docs/reusable-release.md contains the complete before/after install inventory. Both committed locks remain byte-identical to 091124b. No release dispatch, publication or merge performed."
  "2026-11-07T23:46:03.257Z",pi-agent,The new CI lock-smoke shell step also ran unchanged locally under pinned npm 11.21.0 against fresh copies of the current root and private manifests/locks; both installations succeeded. PM linked-test execution uses the default sandbox context; no test-run artifacts are written into the package tracker.
  "2026-11-07T23:51:01.184Z",pi-agent,"PR #260 is ready for review. Initial CI run 42426776935: both new lock compatibility jobs passed (Node 22.18.0 and 26); Windows Node 22 and CodeQL passed. Full Node 26 npm gate found one additional older structural assertion in test/release-continuation-adapter.test.ts that prohibited even the now-required global npm bootstrap (1632 passed, 1 failed, 2 platform skips). Updated that assertion to require the exact pinned script-disabled npm bootstrap and retain the prohibition on all other reconciliation npm installs. Expanding focused coverage to include the adapter suite; fresh exact-head CI will verify the follow-up."
  "2026-11-07T23:52:06.683Z",pi-agent,"Follow-up local verification passes: adapter suite 62/62 with zero failures/skips (via linked pm test), bringing focused coverage to 105 passing tests including the original 43 workflow/runtime tests. Test compilation and typecheck pass after the assertion update. Reconciliation still forbids project npm installs, while requiring the exact verified npm bootstrap. Initial CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42426776935 completed with 4 successful jobs (both lock gates and both Windows consumers) and the 2 Linux test jobs failing only the old adapter assertion. CodeQL passed separately. PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260 will receive fresh exact-head gates; no old-head success is treated as final verification."
  "2026-11-08T00:01:44.834Z",pi-agent,"CI at 66a3a1a: both Linux suites pass 1633 tests with 2 platform skips each and 100% coverage thresholds across 48 measured sources. Both npm gates then refuse the new PowerShell $LASTEXITCODE conditional in ci.yml as an unresolved publish path. Use explicit Bash for Windows npm setup instead, retaining the selected Node global prefix, set -euo pipefail and exact active-version check. npm run verify:release-publish-attestation now passes locally; all three pin/lock regressions pass; typecheck passes. Parser follow-up ops-attestation-powershell-guards tracks the out-of-scope shell-language issue. Windows consumers, lock gates and CodeQL all passed at 66a3a1a; final CI must run again after this change."
  "2026-11-08T03:03:57.816Z",codex-sol,"Re-review class audit: (1) metadata-only recovery must not depend on registry installation; defer reconciliation npm bootstrap into the locked-runtime installer. (2) failure reporting must survive bootstrap and dependency-install failures; attempt the configured alert even when setup fails, without installing locks with bundled npm. (3) bootstrap exceptions must allow exactly one pinned npm install and inspect every command. (4) runtime failure tests must enumerate every reusable and CI setup, including Windows. Searched workflows, scripts, templates, SDK/CLI, JSON/TOON and packed/no-git consumers: the changed paths are release infrastructure; tracker/output contracts remain unaffected. Reusing PR #260 and this item; origin/main is already an ancestor."
  "2026-11-08T03:07:55.575Z",codex-sol,"Revert proof in disposable source copies: restoring only the prior workflow fails the reconciliation/alert assertions; restoring only release-runtime.ts fails the on-demand installer regression. Across all 7 eager reusable setups and all 3 CI setups (including Windows), appended unrelated global installs, removed exact-version guards and swallowed bootstrap failures are detected in 30/30 mutations. Fixed baseline and restored fixed copies pass. Both reconciliation test files inspect all steps without exemptions. The native empty probe still invokes no npm; both on-demand private and trusted-tool installers reject stale/newer npm and install failures before ci. Focused direct run: 107/107 pass, no skips; test compilation passes."
  "2026-11-08T03:26:59.631Z",codex-sol,"Expanded focused linked test run passes 112/112 with zero skips, including both real npm lifecycle/consumer tests and the fixture-precondition suite. First full gate measured all four coverage dimensions at 100% across 48 sources but reported three test failures: a newly introduced literal-name filter violated the existing fixture guard, and the npx bootstrap launcher propagated ignore-scripts into two lifecycle tests. Replaced the selector with one explicit expected name plus an exact per-job cardinality assertion; no existing guard or test was weakened. Full gates now run the cached pinned npm binary directly, without bootstrap-only config leaking into the suite, under isolated Git configuration."
  "2026-11-08T03:44:14.827Z",codex-sol,"Additional class instances found during the package-wide audit: request invokes only Node/GitHub commands and direct HTTP OIDC preflight, so its global npm bootstrap is unnecessary; verify_bun invokes npm only for a configured bunx hook. Removed request bootstrap and guarded Bun bootstrap with the same caller-hook condition as its locked install. Reconciliation/request tests prohibit installation commands in every metadata-only step, and all remaining reusable plus CI setup bodies retain exact-command and four-outcome checks. Interrupted the old Bun gate so final evidence will cover this broader fix; the prior npm gate passed 1635 tests with 2 platform skips, 100% all four dimensions across 48 sources, and all remaining release checks. A separate reused-checkout strict health check reports environment-specific extension-host skew and driver drift; no driver or dependency changes are authorized by this task, and fresh-checkout CI will verify health."
  "2026-11-08T04:08:55.191Z",codex-sol,"Final class fix verified: metadata-only reconcile/request jobs perform no eager npm installation; reconciliation pins npm 11.21.0 only before a missing locked runtime install; Bun bootstrap is conditional on its caller hook; alert scripts are attempted after bootstrap or dependency-install failure, with locked installs allowed only after verified setup. Exact bootstrap-command checks inspect every command in all 6 remaining reusable and 3 CI setups. Final disposable proofs catch 27 bootstrap mutations (extra install, wrong version, swallowed failure), 2 metadata-install mutations and 1 unconditional Bun-bootstrap mutation; both workflow-only and runtime-only reversions also fail, and restored fixed sources pass. Linked focused command passes 112/112, zero skips. On Node 26.13.0 with npm 11.21.0 and isolated Git configuration, npm run release:check and bun run release:check both pass: 1635 passed, 0 failed, 2 platform skips each; 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 48 measured sources, 0% duplication, 371 documented declarations, zero root/private audit vulnerabilities, and all changelog/attestation/lifecycle gates pass. Both locks remain unchanged from 091124b; original real npm 10.9.3 EUSAGE versus npm 11.21.0 lock proof is retained above. PR #260 remains the sole PR. Fresh-checkout CI and automated re-review follow the push; no release, publication or merge was performed. The separate reused-checkout strict-health environment warnings remain documented above."
  "2026-11-08T05:26:07.260Z",codex-sol,"Round 2 rules: local on-demand bootstrap must not require privileges or mutate an inherited global npm; installation-policy guards must recognize every npm install family and alias. Package-wide search found both trusted-tool and private provenance installs share installLockedRuntime. They now use an isolated writable temporary prefix, explicit Node/npm-cli invocation, exact version verification and finally cleanup. Hosted eager workflow setups use their setup-node-owned toolchain prefix and are not local recovery paths. The alias audit also found downgrade and retry detectors in test/release-workflow.test.ts; they now reuse the same installation-command scanner. SDK/CLI, JSON/TOON, packed consumers and non-git tracker paths have no global bootstrap or duplicate install-policy scanner; new runtime tests use non-git temporary source roots. Existing PR and item retained; origin/main is already an ancestor."
  "2026-11-08T05:28:53.592Z",codex-sol,"Round 2 behavioral revert proof in disposable package copies: restoring only installLockedRuntime to the previous implementation makes the on-demand installer regression fail (0/1); the inherited npm explicitly refuses global writes while the fixed path works for both tools and provenance. Restoring only npmInstalls behavior (retaining its new export) makes both the bootstrap/metadata policy corpus and retry-alias regression fail (0/2). Restoring fixed functions passes 1/1 and 2/2 respectively. Policy corpus tries 26 installation spellings in every metadata-only step and all 9 reusable/CI bootstraps, with newline, semicolon and AND separators. All original negative tests remain. Focused direct tests pass 46/46; expanded pinned-pm linked run passes 113/113 with no skips. Typecheck, test compilation and lint pass. Full npm and Bun gates follow with the existing two-worker limit."
  "2026-11-08T05:35:50.620Z",codex-sol,"The follow-on class audit found installation commands behind shell conditionals, assignments, command/env wrappers and npm.cmd would bypass the original first-token check. npmInstalls now uses the existing commandCandidates/commandName/commandArguments parser instead of raw token position. The adversarial corpus covers all 26 install spellings in seven invocation shapes and three separators for every setup, plus all metadata-only steps. The focused suite still passes 46/46 with no skips. Interrupted the first full gate so final evidence covers this additional class fix; no earlier full-gate result is claimed for the new implementation. A real credential-free bootstrap also installed both current production locks successfully and preserved both lock byte sequences."
  "2026-11-08T05:48:09.643Z",codex-sol,"Both final implementation gates passed with Node 26.13.0 and npm 11.21.0 under isolated Git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each report 1636 passed, zero failed, two platform skips; 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 48 sources; zero duplication, 371 documented declarations and zero root/private audit vulnerabilities. A final fetch found new main eec92e0 updating only CodeQL action pins. Merged origin/main without conflicts or tracker-history changes; repeating focused and full gates on the merged branch before push. The final function-only disposable reverts were repeated after the shell-prefix fix: runtime 0/1 and policy scanner 0/2; fixed restoration 1/1 and 2/2."
  "2026-11-08T06:03:03.980Z",codex-sol,"Merged-branch final verification passed after main eec92e0 was merged in 880823f: linked focused suite 113/113, zero skips; npm run release:check and bun run release:check each 1636 passed, zero failed, two platform skips, with at most two test workers and isolated Git configuration. Both full gates retain 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across 48 measured sources, 0% duplication, 371 documented declarations, zero production/private audit vulnerabilities, and passing changelog/attestation/lifecycle checks. Typecheck and test compilation pass. Both locks remain byte-identical to 091124b. Final disposable function reverts fail (runtime 0/1, scanner 0/2), restored functions pass (1/1, 2/2); real local npm bootstrap installs both locks successfully. Existing file/doc/test links cover all changes. Releasing the claim and pushing to the existing PR #260; fresh pushed-head CI and re-review remain pending for the orchestrator. No new item, second PR, release, publication or PR merge. No new PM CLI/SDK bug encountered."
  "2026-11-08T09:50:59.526Z",codex-sol,"Continuation inspected local commits, remote PR #260 and all existing tracker evidence without reading agent transcripts. Last pushed implementation f41da88 has six successful CI matrix jobs plus CodeQL; local main merge 8cd02fe remains unpushed. Current review identifies two remaining availability regressions: dependency-based alerts need a fallback after npm setup failure, and the optional npm hook must not prevent the independent Bun mirror check. Also verifying Windows-compatible local npm invocation. Retaining all valid code and existing follow-up item; no duplicate PR or item."
  "2026-11-08T09:54:25.955Z",codex-sol,"Verified current review findings and fixed both availability paths. The configured alert still runs after setup/install failure; if it fails (including an actual missing dependency), a gh-only fallback deduplicates issues by workflow run, cleans its body file and refuses lookup/create errors. Bun mirror installation and health finish before conditional pinned npm setup and caller acceptance, with scratch tracker/cache context retained through GITHUB_ENV. Windows local runtime uses the bundled npm CLI through the current Node executable for probe/bootstrap rather than invoking npm.cmd without a shell; both trusted-tool and private-runtime locked installs retain the shared implementation. Native Windows CI exercises a disposable lock with an install lifecycle sentinel. No lifecycle guard or lock format changed. Focused initial regression run: 34 passed, zero failed, one native-Windows skip on Linux; typecheck and test compilation pass. Full gates and disposable revert proofs follow."
  "2026-11-08T09:56:37.301Z",codex-sol,"Fresh disposable proof on immutable 091124b under Node 22.18.0: exact production ci exits 1 with npm 10.9.3 (EUSAGE; glob@13.0.6 does not satisfy glob@13.0.7), exits 0 with npm 11.21.0; private provenance lock exits 0 with both. Both current locks equal those fixtures byte-for-byte and all four installs preserve SHA-256. Workflow-only revert for the new alert fallback fails 0/1; restored workflow passes 1/1. Workflow-only revert for Bun independence/order fails 0/2; restored workflow passes 2/2. Expanded pinned-pm linked suite passes 115/115, zero skips. One earlier local run selected the npm package shell wrapper rather than its executable .bin entry; corrected the local invocation and reran successfully. No implementation test was weakened. npm/Bun release gates now run serially with two workers, exact npm 11.21.0, Node 26.13.0 and isolated Git configuration."
  "2026-11-08T10:05:47.251Z",codex-sol,"The first full npm suite passed all 1638 tests (three platform skips) but correctly failed the unchanged 100% branch gate: the new Windows launcher ternaries were not covered on Linux. Extended the existing runtime scenario corpus to exercise both normal PATH-based npm and a disposable Node distribution with adjacent bundled CLI, restoring platform/execPath descriptors in finally. The Windows-shaped case has no npm shim or git on PATH and exercises both trusted-tool and private installers across current/stale/wrong versions, bootstrap failure and ci failure. Focused helper suite now passes 4/4 and scripts/release-runtime.ts measures 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Function-only Windows invocation revert in a disposable copy fails 0/1; fixed restoration passes 1/1. Native Windows CI remains a separate real-platform check. Repeating both complete gates after this test-only correction; thresholds remain unchanged."
  "2026-11-08T10:24:06.680Z",codex-sol,"Final local verification passes after the Windows coverage correction: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each report 1638 passed, zero failed, three platform skips; all four coverage dimensions are 100% across 48 measured sources. Both complete gates pass typecheck/build/test compilation, lint, 0% duplication, documentation for 371 declarations, zero root/private audit vulnerabilities, changelog, publication attestation and lifecycle checks. Expanded pinned-pm linked suite passed 115/115; the extended helper suite passes 4/4 with 100% coverage. Fresh immutable 091124b npm 10.9.3 versus 11.21.0 proof and workflow/function-only revert failures/restorations are recorded above. Both locks remain byte-identical. Existing main merge 8cd02fe and all prior valid commits retained. Pushing this sole branch to ready PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260; fresh final-head CI (including native Windows runtime) and review remain pending at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260/checks. Last pushed-head reviewer quota skips/neutral checks are missing review evidence, not approval. Releasing only this claim; item stays in progress for orchestrator verification. No new PM CLI/SDK bug, duplicate item or PR, release dispatch, publication or PR merge."
  "2026-11-08T15:14:24.110Z",codex-sol,"Round 4 continuation: reused the existing clean remote branch and PR #260; origin/main is already an ancestor. All four findings are valid. General rules: engine compatibility must be checked at the declared Node floor; npm install classification must use the subcommand, never a script argument; install acceptance requires positive dependency evidence; every simulated platform must intercept its executable without reaching host npm. Audit all shared scanner consumers and locked installers, add adversarial regressions and disposable revert proofs, then run both full gates with two workers. Review threads remain open for orchestrator replies."
  "2026-11-08T15:19:41.756Z",codex-sol,"Round 4 class audit: npmInstalls is shared by every reusable/CI bootstrap, metadata-only reconciliation/request guard, publication-downgrade guard and retry-loop guard. Matching now uses the npm subcommand after configuration operands; the adversarial corpus covers all 26 alias spellings across eight command forms and seven non-installing verbs. Runtime executable audit found two additional POSIX-only shims; all three installer fixtures now share PATH plus Node-adjacent CLI interception. Both private provenance and trusted-source installers retain six success/failure scenarios across native and forced Windows routes (24 cases), with no git available. Native install acceptance now verifies a locked local dependency plus root/dependency lifecycle suppression and immutable lock bytes, and runs on every platform. CI adds a distinct strict private-runtime install at the declared Node floor while retaining the exact release-command gate and floating strict jobs. Existing packed npm/Bun consumers already assert installed package and behavioral outcomes; SDK/CLI JSON/TOON and non-git tracker product paths do not invoke these test-only guards, so no tracker/backend contract changes are needed."
  "2026-11-08T15:19:42.653Z",codex-sol,"Round 4 disposable revert proof (review checkout unchanged): (1) removing only the added floor CI step fails every private runtime Node floor has an independent strict engine gate (0/1), restoration passes (1/1); (2) restoring only npm-bootstrap-contract.ts from b235b7b fails npm install and retry guards distinguish every install alias from script and option operands (0/1), restoration passes (1/1); (3) replacing only the private installer invocation with a no-op fails native Windows installs a locked runtime without npm.cmd or lifecycle execution (0/1) on missing installed dependency, restoration passes (1/1); (4) removing only the fixture execPath redirection fails every on-demand locked installer pins npm and refuses bootstrap failures before ci (0/1) on the Windows route, restoration passes (1/1). Each proof ran node --test --test-concurrency=2 with its named test pattern in a disposable source copy. The retained Node-floor adversary also proves EBADENGINE for incompatible root and transitive engine declarations before node_modules writes. Focused integration command passes 119/119, zero failures/skips."
  "2026-11-08T15:20:57.159Z",codex-sol,"Focused suite and pinned-pm linked execution pass 119/119 with zero skips; npm run typecheck and npm run build:test pass. Full npm and Bun release checks will run sequentially with Node 26.13.0, npm 11.21.0, isolated Git configuration and the existing two-worker coverage runner. Native Windows execution will be verified by the expanded Windows CI matrix after push."
  "2026-11-08T15:22:10.130Z",codex-sol,"The first full gate stopped at unchanged 0% duplication: the new tests repeated the existing CI parser declaration. Consolidated all five CI reads into one typed fixture; focused engine regressions pass 2/2 and duplication now reports 0/38141 lines, 144 sources, zero clones. No threshold or existing assertion changed. Full checks are restarted on the consolidated implementation."
  "2026-11-08T15:38:53.384Z",codex-sol,"Round 4 final local acceptance: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both PASS sequentially on Node 26.13.0/npm 11.21.0 with isolated Git configuration and two test workers. Each reports 1644 tests: 1642 pass, zero failures, two existing platform skips; statements/branches/functions/lines each 100% across 48 measured sources. Duplication: zero clones, 0/38141 lines, 144 sources. Docstrings: 371 declarations across 48 files. Root/private audits: zero vulnerabilities; pack, changelog, attestation and lifecycle gates pass. Exact Node 22.18.0 installs of both committed locks with the release command and the additional private engine-strict install all pass without changing lock hashes. Typecheck, test compilation and the 119-test linked focused suite pass. Revert proofs for all four findings are above. Latest fetch confirms origin/main remains an ancestor and the remote PR branch has not moved. Fresh CI after push remains required, especially native Windows; no old-head result certifies this revision. Claim released for orchestrator verification; item remains in progress and review threads remain open."
  "2026-11-09T00:10:41.668Z",pi-glm,"Round 5 re-review plan (head 78dae97, 7 findings). Rules per finding: (1) ci.yml root engines floor — every committed lock the runtime installs gets an engine-strict check at the Node floor; add the root strict install beside the private-runtime one plus structural+behavioral tests. (2) alert fallback dedupe — fallback issue lookup keys on the workflow run identity, not the exact fallback title, so an alert issue that references the failed run (documented contract) suppresses duplication; docs updated. (3) npm bootstrap cache — a package install whose bytes the process executes must not read a cache another local user can pre-populate; replace the fixed shared temp cache with a fresh private mkdtemp cache, always removed. (4) alert test gains the ready/successful-install/failing-script fallback case. (5) install scanner — a value-taking npm option before the subcommand must not hide an install; extend the value-flag set with npm 11 string configs and add corpus cases. (6) installer matrix gains a bootstrap-succeeds-without-CLI case asserting refusal before ci plus cleanup. (7) runtime npm fixture — the Node twin must be creatable without Windows file-symlink privilege; hardlink with copy fallback on win32, symlink elsewhere, plus an executable-twin assertion. Windows CI is the revert witness for (7) since Linux cannot deny symlink privilege."
  "2026-11-09T00:19:09.720Z",pi-glm,"Round 5 fixes and revert proofs (all focused tests on Node 24.19.0): (1) private cache: scripts/release-runtime.ts now bootstraps and installs through a fresh mkdtemp cache (0700) removed on every outcome; reverting to the fixed shared temp cache fails the installer matrix (the fixture's cache recorder ENOENTs on the no-longer-created shared path, and the fresh/private/cleanup assertions fail); restored, 4/4 pass. (2) value-taking options: npm-bootstrap-contract VALUE_FLAGS now carries npm 11 string configs (install-strategy, audit-level, depth, cpu, os, libc, archive, save-prefix, scope, lockfile-version, fetch-*, max-sockets, proxy family, user-agent, local-address, ca/cert/key, git, editor, to/from, search*, node-options); removing install-strategy alone makes the adversarial corpus accept 'npm --install-strategy nested ci' (Missing expected exception, 1 fail); restored, 33/33 pass. (3) alert dedupe: the fallback lookup keys on the run identity (in:title,body <run id>) so a caller alert issue with any title that names the run suppresses the fallback; reverting to exact-title lookup fails the 'deduplicate on the workflow run identity' assertion; restored, 1/1 pass. (4) root engine floor: ci.yml gains 'Check root dependency engines at the Node floor' (strict root install at 22.18.0) beside the private-runtime gate, with structural (both strict gates at the floor) and behavioral (real EBADENGINE on an adversary-modified root manifest, no node_modules written) tests; deleting the step fails both tests (2 fail); restored, 2/2 pass. (5) missing bootstrapped CLI: the installer matrix gains a bootstrap-succeeds-without-CLI case asserting refusal before ci plus prefix and cache cleanup; reverting the fixture to always write the CLI fails it ('Missing expected exception: private/missing'); restored, 4/4 pass. (6) fallback after successful install: the alert matrix gains NPM_READY=true, npm ci succeeds, npm run fails -> fallback issue; the regression that attempts the script only when installation fails makes that case fail; restored, 1/1 pass. (7) Windows fixture: the Node twin is now a hard link (copy fallback across volumes) on win32 and a symlink elsewhere; the suite asserts the twin is executable. Reverting to an unconditional file symlink only reproduces on Windows (EPERM without Developer Mode), so Windows CI running the release-runtime suite on the pushed head is the witness; Linux cannot deny symlink privilege."
  "2026-11-09T01:23:26.309Z",pi-glm,"Round 5 validation on the package worktree: focused suites pass (release-runtime 4/4; daily-release-workflow 33/33; release-workflow + release-continuation-adapter 77/77; typecheck clean). Full gates with isolated git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0, 1645 tests, 1643 pass, 0 fail, 2 platform skips; statements/branches/functions/lines each 100% across 48 sources; duplication 0% (38200 lines, 0 clone pairs); 371 declarations documented; production and release-tools audits clean; pack dry-run, changelog and attestation checks pass. Windows CI on the pushed head is the revert witness for the fixture symlink finding (linux cannot reproduce EPERM)."
  "2026-11-09T01:34:52.967Z",pi-glm,"Windows CI evidence on the pushed round-5 head: the installer matrix and the native Windows locked runtime both pass on Node 22 and 26, so the hardlink Node twin, the private cache and the missing-CLI case all hold on real Windows. The windows jobs still failed on a pre-existing defect from round 3 (already red on the previous head): 'an empty native probe' passes an absolute path to node --import, which the Windows ESM loader rejects (ERR_UNSUPPORTED_ESM_URL_SCHEME). Fixed by passing the preload as a file:// URL; the class audit found the same plain-path --import pattern only in tests whose CI steps run on Linux jobs, where the loader never sees Windows paths."
  "2026-11-09T01:49:28.886Z",pi-glm,"Fresh head evidence (6167cea): all required CI checks pass — test (22) and (26), windows-consumers (22) and (26) (the Windows witness for the fixture twin and the file-URL preload fix; both were failing on the previous head), and Release lock compatibility at both Node floors including the new strict root engine gate; CodeQL and Greptile pass. All seven round-5 review threads were answered with the fix commit and the revert evidence."
  "2026-11-09T06:06:15.193Z",pi-glm,"Round 6 plan (head bb688ba, 6 findings). (3) --location/-L join the scanner's value flags plus corpus cases. (4) npm exec/x with --package/-p are package-acquiring: the install guards and the retry-loop guard (same detector) reject them, while plain 'npm exec <name>' without --package stays allowed per the existing must-allow corpus. (5) the generated bootstrapped CLI records NPM_CONFIG_CACHE per invocation; the matrix asserts the post-bootstrap probe and the ci call both used the private cache. (6) the POSIX PATH fixture npm becomes a quoted sh wrapper (a shebang cannot carry an execPath with spaces) and the matrix bin directory gains a permanent space in its name, so spaces are adversarially exercised on every run. (1)+(2) declined with evidence per the scope control: pinning the caller's Node for the matched CLI and discovering an npm CLI outside the Node directory both need a shim-target discovery mechanism (PATH scan plus cmd parsing or symlink classification) whose success paths cannot be exercised off Windows, conflicting with the 100 percent coverage gate, the no-shell subprocess contract and the ban on trusted sources importing test modules; official Node distributions bundle the npm CLI beside node.exe, which covers every environment the runtime actually executes in. Smallest shipped improvement: a clear refusal naming the requirement when the adjacent CLI is absent on Windows, plus a docs sentence and a follow-up item."
  "2026-11-09T06:12:24.353Z",pi-glm,"Round 6 fixes and revert proofs (focused: release-runtime 5/5, daily+release-workflow 48/48, adapter+runtime 67/67, 115/115 combined, typecheck clean): (3) --location and -L joined the value flags; removing --location alone makes the corpus accept 'npm --location global ci' (Missing expected exception, 3 tests fail combined with (4)). (4) package-acquiring npm exec/x (--package, -p, --package=x, -p=x) are rejected by the install guards and the retry-loop guard, which share the detector; the shell scanner consumes the 'npm exec' pair as a wrapper prefix, so the contract also reads the raw words candidates skip; plain 'npm exec <name>' without --package stays allowed per the existing must-allow corpus, and reverting the acquisition rule fails the retry-guard and alias-distinguish tests. (5) the generated bootstrapped CLI records its cache per invocation; the matrix asserts the post-bootstrap version probe and the ci call both ran through the private cache (per-row expected counts) and reverts to an empty record on removal. (6) the POSIX PATH fixture npm is a quoted sh wrapper (a shebang cannot carry an execPath with spaces) and the matrix permanently runs with a Node executable under 'node with space' plus a 'bin with space' directory; reverting to the shebang fixture fails the installer matrix on this host (kernel splits the spaced interpreter path). (2, partial) the runtime now refuses with a named requirement instead of a confusing ENOENT when no npm CLI sits beside the Node executable on Windows; removing the guard resurfaces the ENOENT and fails the new refusal test; docs describe the bundled-CLI requirement. (1) and (2, mechanism) declined with evidence: pinning the caller's Node for a matched PATH CLI and discovering a CLI outside the Node directory both need a shim-target discovery mechanism whose success paths cannot run off Windows (where.exe semantics, Windows-only shim formats), conflicting with the 100 percent coverage gate, the no-shell subprocess contract and trusted sources importing test modules; official Node distributions bundle the npm CLI beside node.exe, which holds in every environment the runtime executes in (hosted runners, the explicit CI install into the Node directory, local official distributions). Follow-up item recorded for the discovery mechanism."
  "2026-11-09T06:39:17.004Z",pi-glm,"Round 6 validation: focused suites 115/115 (release-runtime 5/5, daily-release-workflow + release-workflow 48/48, adapter 67/67), typecheck clean. Full gates with isolated git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exit 0, 1646 tests, 1644 pass, 0 fail, 2 platform skips; statements/branches/functions/lines 100 percent across 48 sources; duplication 0 percent; 371 declarations documented; audits, pack, changelog and attestation checks pass. Follow-up item ops-3jck records the declined discovery mechanism with its evidence."
  "2026-11-09T06:45:48.070Z",codex-sol,"User-authorized takeover from the quota-exhausted pi agent: inspected clean remote-matching branch and existing PR 260 without reading transcripts. Latest review findings remain valid: Windows file-symlink privileges, duplicate install counting, printed-command false positives and missing-CLI cache cleanup. Completing matching-Node and non-adjacent npm discovery cases with regression and revert evidence. Existing valid fixes and append-only tracker history are preserved."
  "2026-11-09T06:53:28.101Z",codex-sol,"Fresh immutable repro on Node 22.18.0: npm 10.9.3 running ci --omit=dev --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund exits 1 with EUSAGE and the glob 13.0.6/13.0.7 mismatch against 091124b. npm 11.21.0 runs the same command successfully. Both current committed locks also install with that exact command on Node 22.18.0/npm 11.21.0. Historical and current manifest/lock bytes remain unchanged. Latest pinned-pm linked focused suite passes 119/119, zero skips; discovery linked suite passes 6/6. Typecheck and test compilation pass."
  "2026-11-09T06:53:29.439Z",codex-sol,"Disposable revert proofs: restoring the prior install scanner fails the repeated-bootstrap test and, independently, the printed-command test; moving npm CLI resolution outside try leaves a cache and fails the cleanup assertion; restoring the spaced fixture file symlink fails under a privilege-denying preload; restoring the prior runtime fails the caller-Node equality assertion. Each mutated run exits 1, and each restored implementation exits 0. Review mapping for this revision: PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61JKTa and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61JKTd use the matching npm/caller Node discovery regression; PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61Jd_X uses the locked-installer matrix with denied file symlinks; PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61Jd_b and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61Jd_d use the repeated/printed guard regressions; PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61Jd_f uses missing-CLI cleanup. Earlier scanner/cache/spaces fixes from c71f16c are preserved. Threads remain untouched for the orchestrator."
  "2026-11-09T06:56:12.765Z",codex-sol,"Additional local tracker health check reports two existing worktree-environment findings: extension_host_pm_cli_version_skew (pinned host 2026.11.4 versus installed pm-github 2026.11.8) and merge_driver_configuration_drift:5. Item history passes drift validation and every changed history is new or a byte-prefix extension of main. Per scope rules, no dependency bump or shared merge-driver configuration repair was attempted. Fresh CI npm installation remains the tracker-health gate; prior-head CI health passed."
  "2026-11-09T06:59:56.349Z",codex-sol,"The first full npm run passed 1647 tests with zero failures and two platform skips, but correctly failed the unchanged 100 percent branch threshold on the new npm lookup PATH-unset branch. Added PATH-unset coverage to the missing-CLI cleanup regression. Focused runtime c8 now passes 7/7 tests with 100 percent statements, branches, functions and lines. Re-running both complete release gates sequentially on Node 22.18.0 with npm 11.21.0 and isolated git configuration."
  "2026-11-09T07:12:44.435Z",codex-sol,"Final local gates pass on verified Node 22.18.0/npm 11.21.0 with isolated HOME and git configuration: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each report 1647 passing tests, zero failures, two platform skips, and 100 percent statements/branches/functions/lines across 48 measured sources. Duplication is zero; 372 declarations are documented. Both production and private-runtime audits report zero vulnerabilities; changelog, release-date/sections, publish-attestation and lifecycle checks pass. Focused linked suite 119/119 and discovery 6/6 also pass. Both current locks and immutable 091124b manifests/locks remain unchanged. Claims will be released before the final commit; fresh CI for that commit is the remaining full gate, visible at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260/checks. No merge, release dispatch or review-thread changes."
  "2026-11-09T07:20:52.926Z",codex-sol,"CI run 42577915123 on 99edb96 passed both lock jobs and both native Windows consumer jobs. Linux Node 22/26 passed all 1647 tests but failed branch coverage at the POSIX npm symlink-target success path: local runtime layout had exercised that path implicitly, while hosted Node uses an adjacent CLI. Adding a deterministic POSIX discovery fixture. New review PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61KNto also demonstrates timeout duration operands bypass the install guard; adding explicit timeout-wrapper parsing without scanning printed arguments. Existing 30-minute CI observation deadline remains 07:43 UTC."
  "2026-11-09T07:22:26.813Z",codex-sol,"Follow-up focused suite passes 25/25, typecheck and test compilation pass. The timeout guard regression covers direct/command/env/nested wrappers, value-taking timeout options, metadata and bootstrap refusal, retry detection and allowed printed commands. Reverting only the guard to 99edb96 makes the timed-install test fail; restoring passes. A separate deterministic POSIX npm symlink fixture fails when target discovery is removed and passes after restoration. Focused c8 now reports 8/8 runtime tests and four 100 percent coverage dimensions. Re-running both full release gates before the follow-up commit."
  "2026-11-09T07:33:12.341Z",codex-sol,"Follow-up npm run release:check passes on Node 22.18.0/npm 11.21.0: 1649 passing tests, zero failures, two platform skips, four 100 percent coverage dimensions across 48 sources, zero duplication, 372 documented declarations and zero vulnerabilities in both audits; all remaining gates pass. Focused linked suite passes 121/121 without skips. Timed-install and deterministic symlink revert proofs both fail on removal and pass after restoration. Current follow-up Bun gate is running; the earlier implementation Bun gate passed in full. Publishing this follow-up now permits fresh exact-head CI before the existing 07:43 UTC observation cutoff; final Bun and CI receipts will be recorded in the PR description and final handoff. Prior CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42577915123 passed locks, native Windows and all tests but failed only the now-deterministically-tested symlink branch. Final-head checks: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260/checks. Claim released, item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-11-09T07:41:57.831Z",codex-sol,"Final follow-up Bun run release:check also passes: 1649 passing tests, zero failures, two platform skips, four 100 percent coverage dimensions across 48 measured sources; all audit, changelog, attestation, lifecycle and duplication gates pass. This matches the final npm gate on implementation commit 89a857ef7a7bff5cb3cf9b413c745b9f8f277376. At the original observation cutoff, exact implementation CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42580124245 has passed the Node 22.18.0 lock job and Windows 22 consumers; Linux 26 is in the Bun gate, Linux 22 is in the npm gate, and the remaining lock/Windows jobs are still running. CodeQL run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/actions/runs/42580124334. Remaining checks are pending evidence, not approval. A final tracker receipt commit preserves these results without changing implementation; its fresh checks remain visible at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-ops/pull/260/checks. Both claims remain released; neither item is closed. Review thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61KNto is fixed by 89a857e with the timed-install regression and failing-on-revert proof. CI symlink-branch failure is fixed by the deterministic POSIX discovery test in the same commit. All earlier thread-to-fix mappings remain recorded and will be included in the final handoff; no thread reply or resolution was performed."
  "2026-11-09T09:41:38.305Z",codex-sol,"Final authorized round: remote and local heads match 0eb95e3, PR 260 exists, and origin/main is already an ancestor. Reuse both existing items. Fix only PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61MCRs, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61MCRR, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61MCRa, PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61MCRj and PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61MCSF. The existing required test matrix will aggregate both release-lock results and explicitly fail on non-success, avoiding skipped required jobs. Exact-floor provenance and full-development engine checks run in the existing 22.18.0 release-lock job. npm argv classification remains deferred to issue 263. Targeted gates only; CI certifies the full gate. No review thread writes."
  "2026-11-09T09:43:53.989Z",codex-sol,"IMPORTANT thread PRRT_kwDOTOTl1M61MCRs revert proof: disposable source copy, node --test --test-concurrency=2 --test-name-pattern=\"matching npm\" test/release-runtime.test.ts: fixed 1/1 pass; reverting only return resolve(candidate) to return candidate gives 0/1 and MODULE_NOT_FOUND after the child cwd changes; restoring gives 1/1 pass. Relative-PATH coverage extends the existing matching-npm regression. Bootstrap matrix now also asserts the generated version probe and ci use the distinct caller Node. Targeted typecheck, test compilation and lint pass. Existing strict-engine assertion updated from two checks to three for the new development check."
  "2026-11-09T09:45:56.473Z",codex-sol,"Final-round targeted evidence: pinned-pm linked command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-runtime.test.ts test/daily-release-workflow.test.ts test/release-workflow.test.ts test/release-continuation-adapter.test.ts passes 120/120 with zero skips; runtime-only linked suite passes 7/7. node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-provenance.test.ts on exact Node 22.18.0 passes 5/5. npm run typecheck, npm run build:test and npm run lint pass. Parsed CI YAML confirms release-lock matrix 22.18.0/26 feeds both required test jobs; executing the first gate step accepts success and refuses failure, cancelled and skipped. Both new floor steps use the exact 22.18.0 condition. The broader 121-test attempt had 120 passes and one existing real-install test fail on npm registry ETIMEDOUT during bootstrap, not an assertion regression. Full release gates remain for final-head CI. No argv classification change, new pm item, second PR or review-thread write."
  "2026-11-09T09:47:04.109Z",codex-sol,"Additional targeted install receipt: reran node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/release-runtime-windows.test.ts with the caller Node hard-linked beside a disposable npm 11.21.0 installation. It passes 1/1, zero skips, using the real locked local dependency and verifying lifecycle suppression and unchanged lock bytes. This isolates the earlier registry-bootstrap ETIMEDOUT from locked installation correctness; it does not certify native Windows on this Linux host. Code fix commit 44b962f addresses all five final-round threads. npm run changelog:full and npm run changelog:check passed after the claim releases; regenerate/check again after this final evidence comment. Final-head CI remains required; no full release gate was rerun locally."
